  "slug": "transfer-molecular-ec8b",
  "summary": "Ultrafast optical and terahertz methods now resolve nonadiabatic strong-field dynamics in NiPS3 and Sr2CuO3 under intense driving.",
  "synthesis": "Three preprints address nonadiabatic light-driven dynamics in correlated insulators, with different emphasis. The NiPS3 study uses time-resolved optical spectroscopy to report nonadiabatic quantum tunneling and ponderomotive blue-shifted resonances near the Keldysh regime. The Sr2CuO3 study, combining experiment and simulation, reports non-integer, blueshifted high harmonic generation driven by mid-infrared pulses, which it attributes to many-body nonadiabatic gating. The Yb-laser terahertz platform is methodological: it combines multi-pass-cell compression, spintronic THz generation and air-biased detection over a broad bandwidth, offering a measurement route suited to such nonequilibrium studies. The new element is the joint treatment of tunneling and harmonic response in driven correlated insulators, probed with broadband, high-sensitivity techniques.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
